{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation evidence (committed at `764af7abb76`)\n\n**Integration pair proven separately** — AC \"`pytest tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py -m \"\"` green\", the command `make verify` can never run because `make test` selects `not integration`:\n\n```\npytest tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py -m \"\" -q\n23 passed, 1 skipped in 41.17s\n```\n\n**Zero paired twins remain**: `git ls-files` prints nothing for all 17 deleted `_heldout.py` paths.\n\n**Mechanism-delta**: `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits **0** — `active=648 new=28 increased=0 stale=0`. `--update-stale` was not run and was not needed; these pairs hold no autouse fixture, so this story drains no baseline row. `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` is green (33 passed), which is the stronger baseline-vs-live-tree assertion.\n\n**Bridge-vocabulary guard**: `test_bridge_status_heldout.py` and `test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py` are both untracked; `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status.py` survives; `pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py` → 9 passed.\n\n**Deleted-filename sweep** — the full word-anchored sweep across the whole tree for all 17 basenames, excluding `.test_durations`, now returns exactly **2** hits, both the frozen corpora already recorded in the \"Frozen literals for the deleted-filename sweep\" comment above:\n\n- `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_02.json:99` (`test_bridge_cli_heldout.py`)\n- `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/prose.json:22` (`test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py`)\n\nThe other 15 basenames return 0.\n\nNote on the provenance lines: the merge writes `merged from test_<base>_heldout` WITHOUT the `.py` extension. Naming the module rather than a path is both accurate (the file is gone, so the path no longer resolves) and keeps the merge from re-introducing a deleted filename that this AC sweeps for. An earlier draft wrote the full filename and so failed this AC with 34 self-inflicted hits.\n\n`make verify` is running; its result will be recorded before the change is pushed.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793500890942227167,"uuid":"04f7ea77-3e8d-4d9a-8dd5-65e50fc6b9ba"}